I have reviewed the uploaded document. My assessment is that it is **methodologically strong and should be preserved as a research artifact**, but it should **not be promoted into KnowledgeOS Theory v1.2 or the minimum Kernel definition yet**.

### 1. The central distinction is correct

The strongest result is the separation of:

$$
\boxed{
\text{Algebraic Zero}
\neq
\text{Representational Absence}
\neq
\text{Preservation-relative Zero}
}
$$

The document explicitly states that \(0_i\), \(\varnothing\), and preservation-relative Zero must not be identified without a structure-preserving correspondence. 

That fits very well with the conclusions we reached from the algebraic-structure review.

In particular:

$$
0_i\in D_i
$$

is an **algebraic object**.

Whereas

$$
k_i=\varnothing
$$

is a **representation condition**.

And

$$
Zero_{T,\Pi}(S;D)
\iff
\Pi(T(D))=\Pi(T(E_S(D)))
$$

is an **observational/preservation judgment**.

These belong to different mathematical levels.

