## 2. I agree with keeping HZ4 as the decisive experiment

This is the most scientifically valuable part:

$$
P_S^0:K\rightarrow K
$$

versus

$$
P_S^{restrict}:K\rightarrow K_S
$$

and testing:

$$
O_Q(P_S^0(K))
\stackrel{?}{=}
O_Q(P_S^{restrict}(K)).
$$

The document correctly warns that success would establish only **observational equivalence under the tested observation family**, not that algebraic zero is intrinsically the correct representation of omission. 

That distinction is essential.

I would therefore make HZ4 the **primary experiment**, with HZ1–HZ3 subordinate.

