# 5. One important additional correction

I would tighten one thing further.

The document writes:

$$
K^{(r)}=\prod_iD_i^{(r)}.
$$

This should remain explicitly a **candidate representation model**, not a definition of the KnowledgeOS state.

Otherwise we risk repeating the same problem we just encountered with

$$
K=(A,R,E).
$$

There are now three distinct levels:

```text
KnowledgeOS semantic state
        │
        ▼
representation at resolution r
        │
        ▼
product / coordinate representation
```

So I would write:

$$
\rho_r: \mathcal S\rightarrow K^{(r)}
$$

and only then, if justified,

$$
K^{(r)}\cong\prod_iD_i^{(r)}.
$$

This is important because **product decomposition is a representation theorem/candidate**, not automatically an ontology of KnowledgeOS.

