## My overall verdict

**Keep it. Do not canonicalize it. Run HZ4 first.**

And I would add one methodological sentence to the research protocol:

$$
\boxed{
\text{A representation-level algebraic property is not a KnowledgeOS semantic law unless its invariance under admissible representations is demonstrated.}
}
$$

That sentence connects this Zero research directly to the algebraic lesson we just established: **KnowledgeOS must derive its algebra, rather than inherit an algebra merely because one representation happens to possess it.**

This also means the Zero/Zoom work can proceed **in parallel with the Minimum Kernel Reduction**, without contaminating the Kernel derivation with an unproven algebraic primitive.
